        "text": "A Climate"
      },
      {
        "y": 94.9,
        "x0": 126.9,
        "x1": 464.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Travelling from north to south in Nigeria, you pass through a fascinating series of"
      },
      {
        "y": 105.7,
        "x0": 131.9,
        "x1": 466.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "landscapes. Rainfall1 in the south-east can be extremely high in the wet season,"
      },
      {
        "y": 117.7,
        "x0": 136.9,
        "x1": 488.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "whereas the northern part of the country is arid2 and prone to3 drought4 during the"
      },
      {
        "y": 130.9,
        "x0": 142.9,
        "x1": 190.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "dry season."
      },
      {
        "y": 149.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 the amount of rain that falls, for example in a month or in a year 2 dry 3 tending to have a particular"
      },
      {
        "y": 161.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 294.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "negative characteristic 4 long period without rain"
      },
      {
        "y": 179.3,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 158.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Vegetation"
      },
      {
        "y": 203.3,
        "x0": 126.9,
        "x1": 503.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "More than 30% of the landscape of Canada lies inside the Arctic Circle, where the land can"
      },
      {
        "y": 214.2,
        "x0": 131.9,
        "x1": 486.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "stay frozen for up to nine months of the year. In these regions, known as the tundra1,"
      },
      {
        "y": 226.2,
        "x0": 137.9,
        "x1": 496.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "vegetation2 is limited. Further south, dense, coniferous3 forests known as taiga cover"
      },
      {
        "y": 239.3,
        "x0": 142.9,
        "x1": 507.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "large areas of land. Towards the border with the United States are the grasslands of the"
      },
      {
        "y": 250.2,
        "x0": 147.9,
        "x1": 328.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "prairies4 and the mixed, temperate forests."
      },
      {
        "y": 282.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 503.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 area in the north with no trees and permanently frozen ground 2 plant life 3 trees that are evergreen"
      },
      {
        "y": 294.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 502.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[in leaf all year round] and produce cones, unlike deciduous trees, which lose their leaves in winter 4 flat"
      },
      {
        "y": 307.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 458,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "grasslands in Canada and northern USA (similar to steppes in Asia or pampas in South America)"
      },
      {
        "y": 324.6,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 161.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Agriculture"
      },
      {
        "y": 348.8,
        "x0": 126.9,
        "x1": 469,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Rice is the main crop grown in the south of China, along with tea, cotton, fruit and"
      },
      {
        "y": 359.6,
        "x0": 131.9,
        "x1": 504.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "vegetables. The rice is planted in flooded paddy fields1. A good year can see two crops of"
      },
      {
        "y": 372.8,
        "x0": 136.9,
        "x1": 512.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "rice and one of vegetables harvested. In the drier, hillier north and west, farmers generally"
      },
      {
        "y": 383.6,
        "x0": 142.9,
        "x1": 448.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "harvest a single crop of cereals2 and, in addition, tend3 sheep and cattle."
      },
      {
        "y": 408,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 fields planted with rice growing in water 2 type of grass cultivated to produce a grain, e.g. a food plant like"
      },
      {
        "y": 420,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 237.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "rice, wheat or maize 3 take care of"
      },
      {
        "y": 438.2,
        "x0": 74.4,
        "x1": 146.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "D Industry"
      },
      {
        "y": 461.1,
        "x0": 126.9,
        "x1": 513.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "France is one of the world’s leading developed1 nations. It is home to large manufacturing2,"
      },
      {
        "y": 474.2,
        "x0": 131.9,
        "x1": 503.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "steel and chemical industries. The country is an important and major producer of aircraft"
      },
      {
        "y": 485.1,
        "x0": 137.9,
        "x1": 489.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "and cars and is at the forefront3 of technology and engineering. Its sizeable nuclear"
      },
      {
        "y": 497.1,
        "x0": 142.9,
        "x1": 506.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "industry generates4 a significant proportion of the nation’s electrical power. Like many"
      },
      {
        "y": 509.1,
        "x0": 147.9,
        "x1": 499.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "developed countries, France provides a lot of help and aid to developing5 countries."
      },
      {
        "y": 540.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 494.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 with a modern, industrial economy 2 producing goods in large numbers 3 in an important position"
      },
      {
        "y": 552.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 494.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 produces/creates 5 describes a country that is poor and does not have a modern, industrial economy"
      },
      {
        "y": 570.5,
        "x0": 75.4,
        "x1": 160.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "E Population"
      },
      {
        "y": 593.5,
        "x0": 126.9,
        "x1": 502.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Brazil is a vibrant mixture of peoples. Some are descended from1 indigenous2 tribes, others"
      },
      {
        "y": 606.7,
        "x0": 131.9,
        "x1": 515.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from the Portuguese, who were the colonial power in Brazil for 300 years. Many Brazilians have"
      },
      {
        "y": 617.5,
        "x0": 136.9,
        "x1": 506,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "African ancestors3 brought over in the 17th century as slaves to work on sugar plantations."
      },
      {
        "y": 629.5,
        "x0": 142.9,
        "x1": 486.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "During the 20th century, large numbers of European migrants4 settled5 in the south."
      },
      {
        "y": 659.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 are related to someone who lived in the past 2 existing naturally in that place 3 relatives from earlier"
      },
      {
        "y": 671.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "times: we are our ancestors’ descendants 4 people who move to live in another country or another part"
      },
      {
        "y": 684.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of their own country (often for reasons of economic need; an emigrant is someone who leaves a country, an"
      },
      {
        "y": 695.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 392.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "immigrant is someone who moves to live in a country) 5 made their homes"
      }
